WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.430
- [Narrator] In 2008,

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:05.100
Samsung's smartphone
manufacturing facilities

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.740
were scattered throughout Mainland China.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.310
Just 15 years later, those
factories have disappeared

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.880
and nearly all of them have
relocated to Southeast Asia.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.280
- It may have given Samsung
a competitive advantage

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.560
to go to Vietnam first.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.600
- [Narrator] But Apple was on its heels.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.515
Over the last few years, the tech giant

00:00:23.515 --> 00:00:27.360
started making similar moves
to diversify its operations.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.306
Here's a closer look at how Samsung

00:00:29.306 --> 00:00:32.340
and Apple's manufacturing moves from China

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.856
are reshaping their businesses,

00:00:33.856 --> 00:00:35.648
and what the strategies reveal

00:00:35.648 --> 00:00:39.240
about the rapidly shifting
global supply chain.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.030
In 2008, Samsung set up a plant

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.220
in the Bac Ninh region of Vietnam

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.470
to reduce its dependence on China.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.800
Tech industry analysts say it
was a forward thinking move

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.390
for the South Korean company.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.440
- They benefited in a lot of ways.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.530
They benefit from cheaper labor
in some of these countries

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.370
that they're moving to.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.770
They benefit from being insulated

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.390
from some of the geopolitical tensions

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:02.280
that come with operating in China

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.930
and continuing to expand in China.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.910
They also benefit from being insulated

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.010
from the kinds of supply
chain shocks that we saw

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:11.070
during the COVID lockdowns in China

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.830
and the supply chain disruptions
that resulted from that.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.970
- [Narrator] Over the next decade,

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.880
rising labor and operating costs in China

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.360
made it difficult for Samsung
to produce its phones cheaply.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.940
That coupled with intensifying competition

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.650
from domestic smartphone rivals

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:29.010
led Samsung's market
share in China to plummet.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.350
Meanwhile, the company was slowly moving

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.630
its smartphone operations
out of the country.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:36.990
Since 2013, the number of
Samsung employees in China

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.570
has fallen by 70%.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.670
Samsung still kept significant

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.920
manufacturing centers in China,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.688
including for its expansive
memory chip business.

00:01:46.688 --> 00:01:47.880
(whooshing sound)

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.710
- [Advertiser] Samsung semiconductor.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.808
- [Narrator] But moving
its smartphone operations

00:01:51.808 --> 00:01:53.700
meant to the company was shielded

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.390
from many of the Trump era
tariffs on Chinese made goods.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.602
- Those tariffs coupled with
the geopolitical tensions

00:01:59.602 --> 00:02:02.340
developing between the
Western world and China

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.491
led a lot of companies to reconsider

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.510
where they're manufacturing things.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.160
- [Narrator] By 2019, it had-

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.860
- Shut its last phone factory

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.080
in the world's biggest smartphone market.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.300
- [Narrator] One year
later, the pandemic hit

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.220
propelling tech companies like Apple

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.590
to make similar moves away from China.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.111
- China had a very strict COVID policy

00:02:22.111 --> 00:02:26.490
that led to a lot of disruption
for many of these companies,

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.310
and seriously pushed them to consider

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:32.400
manufacturing elsewhere
where that kind of disruption

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.430
would be less of a thorn in their sides.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.650
- [Narrator] Apple's plans
gained even more momentum

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.970
in late 2022 after violent
protests rocked the company's

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:45.724
largest iPhone manufacturing
plant in Guangzhou, China.

00:02:45.724 --> 00:02:47.880
(rioter speaking in Chinese)

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.950
Demonstrations erupted when the workers

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.830
who had been under strict
COVIDS lockdown for weeks

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:55.200
learned bonus payments would be delayed.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.320
At the time, Apple said it
was working with the facility

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.050
to ensure employee
concerns were addressed.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.880
According to analysts and people

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.320
in the company's supply chain,

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.270
Apple no longer feels comfortable

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:09.390
having so much of its
business tied up in one place.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:10.620
While different events

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.380
first propelled Samsung
and Apple out of China,

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.770
their new supply chain strategies
focus on the same places,

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:18.330
India and Vietnam.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.034
- These countries, some of
them have offered tax breaks

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:24.150
to companies to locate
their manufacturing.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:27.540
There have been, in some cases,
grants and other incentives

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.240
that are hard for these
companies to pass up.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.420
- [Narrator] Samsung pays
about 10% corporate income tax

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.050
in Vietnam versus China's
standard 25% rate.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.570
It now produces half of
its smartphones there.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.390
Apple also has operations in Vietnam.

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:45.120
The company started producing
its watches in the country

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.913
and moved some iPad
manufacturing there too.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:52.950
In Apple's most recent list
of its top 200 suppliers,

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.530
25 were in Vietnam.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:58.473
That's 25% higher than four years ago.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.870
Then, there's India.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:04.560
Around 20 to 30% of all
of Samsung smartphones

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.590
are now manufactured there,
according to Morgan Stanley,

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:09.420
and it's still expanding.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.503
In 2022, it opened the world's
largest mobile phone factory

00:04:13.503 --> 00:04:14.730
near New Delhi.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.790
These moves helped the company
to become a dominant force

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.280
in India's rapidly
growing smartphone market.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.130
The second largest in
the world behind China.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:25.080
- [Advertiser] Awesome Galaxy A14 5G.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.970
Now at just rupees 44 per day.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:31.050
- [Narrator] In 2022, Samsung
accounted for around 20%

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.030
of the country's total market share

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:35.610
while Apple held less than 4%.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.380
Apple is working to change that.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.470
In a recent earnings
call, CEO Tim Cook said.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:44.340
- India is an incredibly exciting market.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.110
It's a major focus for us.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:50.250
- So, this year Apple has
said it plans to manufacture

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:54.240
a portion of its iPhone 14 models in India

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.850
for the first time which
is a significant move.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.770
You know, the company
is essentially saying

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.650
that we wanna diversify.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.870
- [Narrator] Tech analysts
say manufacturing iPhones

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.210
in India and then selling
them to the surrounding

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:09.090
Southeast Asian market ensures a smooth

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:11.700
and more resilient supply chain.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.230
Apple's longer term goal

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.920
is to ship 40 to 45%
of iPhones from India,

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.050
according to supply chain analysts.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:22.260
In 2022, that number
was in the single digits

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.400
for the company.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.400
More recently, the company
started moving manufacturing

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.900
even closer to home.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.985
A multi-billion dollar deal
with US Chipmaker Broadcom

00:05:30.985 --> 00:05:33.900
will allow Apple to source
critical chip components

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.380
from manufacturing hubs around the US.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.930
But even as Apple and
Samsung spend billions

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:41.160
to move away from China,

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:44.490
the manufacturers may still
depend on suppliers there.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:48.210
During the height of the 2020
COVID19 outbreak in China,

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:50.130
Samsung found itself scrambling

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:52.920
to secure suddenly scarce
Chinese components.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.270
- There's also a political challenge

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:56.250
because these companies many of them

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.740
still need to manufacture
in China to some extent,

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:00.090
and they need to be delicate

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.970
about how they handle
diversifying their supply chains.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:04.500
- [Narrator] Even though
a supply chain shift

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:05.850
won't happen overnight,

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:08.580
Samsung and Apple's
manufacturing strategies

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:10.860
reveal a larger de-risking trend

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.720
that's transforming global markets.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.540
- It's kind of like diversifying
a portfolio, if you will.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.550
Increasingly, as the US and China,

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:19.560
that relationship becomes more contentious

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:23.310
and a lot of western companies
see China as more risky.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.380
And so, they're thinking
about doing less in China.

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:28.890
They're thinking about
de-risking from the perspective

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:31.316
of the politics in this situation.

00:06:31.316 --> 00:06:34.483
(gentle upbeat music)

